  "mechanismSummary": "Hydroxide removes an N–H proton from acetophenone hydrazone, and water protonates the carbon, giving an alkyl diazene. Removing the second N–H proton expels N₂ and leaves a carbanion, which water protonates. Overall the C=O of the ketone (via its hydrazone) becomes CH₂: ethylbenzene.",
